    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract thinking and practical problem-solving—something I enjoy when it’s applied to real-world contexts, like economics or travel planning. My self-employed work often requires calculations, so it’s both useful and engaging for me. However, its rigidity can sometimes feel restrictive compared to the fluidity of history or art.",
